  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Which of the following expressions gives all of the zeros of the function $f(x)=4\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(3x+\\pi )?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.",
  "worked_solution": "The zeros of $y=\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x$ are given by \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the zeros of $f(x)=4\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(3x+\\pi ),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(3x+\\pi ).$ This gives\n\n$$\n3x+\\pi =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+\\pi  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ 3x & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi -\\pi  \\\\ 3x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{n\\pi }{3},$ where $n$ is an integer.",
